flowchart TB
  accTitle: Communication patterns the prompt aims to encourage
  accDescr: Three examples illustrate the intended change in responses: clarify shared state versus instance limits before a singleton, ask for profiling before optimization, and evaluate access patterns, memory caching, and operational costs before Redis. These are examples, not guaranteed outcomes.
  subgraph singleton["Scenario 1 · Write a singleton"]
    direction TB
    singletonTask["Write a singleton pattern for me"]
    singletonDefault["Example to avoid<br/>Provide singleton code immediately"]
    singletonPrompt["Desired example<br/>Shared state or a limit on instances?"]
    singletonTask --> singletonDefault
    singletonTask --> singletonPrompt
  end
  subgraph performance["Scenario 2 · Optimize performance"]
    direction TB
    performanceTask["Optimize this code's performance"]
    performanceDefault["Example to avoid<br/>Suggest several micro-optimizations"]
    performancePrompt["Desired example<br/>Have you profiled it? Where is the bottleneck?"]
    performanceTask --> performanceDefault
    performanceTask --> performancePrompt
  end
  subgraph caching["Scenario 3 · Add Redis caching"]
    direction TB
    cachingTask["Use Redis for caching"]
    cachingDefault["Example to avoid<br/>Provide Redis integration code"]
    cachingPrompt["Desired example<br/>What is the access pattern? Is memory enough?<br/>Can you accept the operational costs?"]
    cachingTask --> cachingDefault
    cachingTask --> cachingPrompt
  end
